---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'Privacy — Rate My Gov';
const description =
  'What Rate My Gov stores and does not store, how hashed identifiers are treated, cookies, Cloudflare Turnstile, retention, and how to contact us.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical="https://ratemygov.in/privacy">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <p>For each vote, we store only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the selected state or Union Territory;</li>
      <li>the choice — satisfied or dissatisfied;</li>
      <li>a timestamp of when the vote was recorded;</li>
      <li>a keyed hash of a random device identifier;</li>
      <li>a keyed hash of the IP address (IPv6 addresses are reduced to their
        /64 network before hashing);</li>
      <li>an approximate state inferred from the connection, used only for
        geolocation flagging.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we do not store</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>your name, phone number, or email address;</li>
      <li>your raw IP address;</li>
      <li>your GPS location or any precise location;</li>
      <li>any account, profile, comment, or other user-generated content.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No account is required to vote, and voting does not create a profile.</p>

    <h2>Hashed identifiers are still personal data</h2>
    <p>
      The hashed device identifier and the keyed hash of the IP address are
      stored to prevent duplicate votes. Hashing makes them difficult to reverse,
      but it is <strong>not</strong> anonymization: these hashes are still treated
      as personal data, protected accordingly, and never exposed publicly. Never
      treat a hash as proof of anonymity.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We set a single device cookie used only for duplicate-vote prevention. It
      is <code>HttpOnly</code>, sent over <code>Secure</code> connections in
      production, and restricted with an appropriate <code>SameSite</code>
      policy. We do not use advertising, analytics, or tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
    <p>
      To limit automated abuse, the vote form may use Cloudflare Turnstile.
      Turnstile loads only when the form is first interacted with. Cloudflare may
      process limited information from your browser (such as IP address and
      browser characteristics) to determine whether the interaction is from a
      human. That processing is governed by Cloudflare's
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.
      We do not receive or store the raw browsing data Turnstile collects.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Vote records are retained for as long as the service operates. There is
      currently no automatic deletion schedule for vote records, and we state
      this plainly rather than promising a fixed retention period. Raw IP
      addresses and raw device identifiers are never stored. If you believe a
      record relates to you and you want it deleted, contact us below and we
      will consider your request.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests, email:
      <a href="mailto:privacy@ratemygov.in">privacy@ratemygov.in</a>.
      <em>(Placeholder address — this mailbox is not yet active.)</em>
    </p>

    <h2>Legal note — DPDP Act, 2023</h2>
    <p>
      This notice references the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 of
      India. <strong>It has not yet been reviewed by legal counsel and is not a
      claim of compliance</strong> with the Act. We are reviewing our practices
      against the Act's requirements and will update this page as that review
      progresses.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>